// How Cloudflare serves the site: the built files in dist/, as static assets on a Worker with no
// code of its own. Any address that is not a file gets index.html, so the app's own screens load
// on a refresh or from a shared link. The headers come from dist/_headers, which the build writes
// from scripts/security-headers.ts. Deploys run from main through Workers Builds (see README).
// Wrangler itself is not a dependency: the deploy command pins it, so its own tooling never
// enters this project's dependency tree or its audit.
{
  "name": "shumar",
  "compatibility_date": "2026-10-11",
  "assets": {
    "directory": "./dist",
    "not_found_handling": "single-page-application",
  },
}
